{"id":"867ad3ab-e943-47c1-9ed8-9e16586ef760","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.016","title":"Industrialization drives convergent microbiome and host physiological shifts in the human metaorganism","title_zh":"工业化驱动人类宿主—微生物复合体（metaorganism）中微生物组和宿主生理的趋同转变","doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.016","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.016","abstract":"Understanding how industrialization reshapes the human metaorganism requires integrating microbiome ecology with host physiology across globally diverse populations. Here, we generate multivariate data from the Global Microbiome Conservancy cohort, including gut microbiome, immunoglobulin A (IgA) sequencing, host genotyping, diet, lifestyle, and fecal biomarker profiles, to investigate host-microbiome interactions across gradients of industrialization and geography. We show that industrialization is associated with homogenized microbial compositions, reduced microbial diversity, and lower community stability, independent of host confounders. We further show that industrialization is linked to elevated markers of gut stress, increased IgA secretion, and altered patterns of IgA-bacteria interactions. Finally, we show that microbiome-based disease predictors trained on industrialized populations are uninformative in less industrialized cohorts, highlighting limited cross-population transferability. Together, our results reveal coordinated restructuring of the microbial ecosystem and host physiology and emphasize the need for inclusive, globally representative data to improve translational microbiome applications across diverse human populations.","abstract_zh":"理解工业化如何重塑人类宿主—微生物复合体（metaorganism），需要在全球多样人群中整合微生物组生态学与宿主生理。在此，我们利用全球微生物保存库队列生成多维数据，包括肠道微生物组、免疫球蛋白A（IgA）测序、宿主基因型、饮食、生活方式和粪便生物标志物，以研究沿工业化和地理梯度的宿主-微生物相互作用。我们表明，工业化与微生物组成的同质化、微生物多样性降低和社区稳定性下降有关，且独立于宿主混杂因素。此外，我们发现工业化与肠道压力标志物升高、IgA分泌增加以及IgA-细菌相互作用模式改变有关。最后，我们表明，在工业化人群训练的基于微生物组的疾病预测模型在非工业化队列中无法提供信息，这突显了跨人群可迁移性的有限性。总之，我们的结果揭示了微生态系统和宿主生理的协调重塑，并强调了需要包容性的、全球代表性的数据，以改善跨多样化人群的转化性微生物组应用。","snippet":"Understanding how industrialization reshapes the human metaorganism requires integrating microbiome ecology with host physiology across globally diverse populations. Here, we generate multivariate data from the Global Microbiome Conservancy cohort, including gut microbiome, immunoglobulin A (IgA) sequencing, host genotyping, diet, lifestyle, and fecal biomarker profiles, to investigate host-microbiome interactions a…","translated_at":"2026-11-10T03:19:17.154541Z","translation_model":"nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":null,"issue":null,"published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-11-10T00:01:10Z","display_date":"2026-11-10T00:01:10Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":null,"print_published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Mathilde Poyet","authors_text":"Mathilde Poyet, Malte Rühlemann, Ana P. Schaan, Yue Ma, Lucas Moitinho-Silva, Eike M. Wacker, Hannah Jebens, Lucas Patel, Le Thanh Tu Nguyen, Alexis Zimmer, Damian Plichta, Daniel McDonald, Christine Stevens, Adwoa Agyei, Mary Y. Afihene, Shadrack O. Asibey, Yaw A. Awuku, Aida S. Badiane, Chris Corzett, Awa Deme, Manuel Dominguez-Rodrigo, Amoako Duah, Alain Fezeu, Alain Froment, Sean Gibbons, Catherine Girard, Jeff Hooker, Fatimah Ibrahim, Deborah Iqaluk, Vanessa Juimo, Pinja Kettunen, Sophie Lafosse, Ernest Lango-Yaya, Soo C. Lee, Jenni Lehtimäki, Yvonne A.L. Lim, Audax Mabulla, Varocha Mahachai, Rihlat S. Mohamed, Katya Moniz, Ivan E. Mwikarago, Yvonne A. Nartey, Daouda Ndiaye, Mary Noel, Charles Onyekwere, Tan M. Pin, Amelie Plymoth, Lewis Roberts, Lasse Ruokolainen, John Rusine, Laure Segurel, B. Jesse Shapiro, Shani Sigwazi, Ainara Sistiaga, Kenneth Valles, Tommi Vatanen, Ratha-korn Vilaichone, Philip Rosenstiel, John Baines, Andre Franke, David Ellinghaus, Rob Knight, Mark Daly, Ramnik J. Xavier, Eric J. Alm, Mathieu Groussin","authors":[{"position":0,"given_name":"Mathil